# YouTube Shorts / Instagram Reels Workflow

This repo is used to produce short-form videos (YouTube Shorts + Instagram Reels) using HeyGen for AI voice.

## When the user provides video content, ALWAYS deliver these 3 things (in this order):

1. **Video Title** — catchy, SEO-friendly, under 70 chars, hook-driven.
2. **HeyGen Voice Script** — follow `voice-script.mdc` rules.
3. **YouTube Description** — follow `description.mdc` rules.

## Output Format

- Use clear markdown headings (`## 1. Title`, `## 2. Voice Script`, `## 3. Description`).
- Voice script must be in a single paragraph block (no bullets, no line breaks).
- Description block should be copy-paste ready (no extra commentary inside it).

## After Delivering Output

- Save the entry under `memory/videos/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` using `memory/templates/video-template.md`.
- This builds a searchable archive of past videos for tone consistency and topic reuse.

## Tone Defaults (unless user overrides)

- Storytelling, humanistic, conversational — never sounds like AI.
- Hook in the first 3 seconds.
- One clear takeaway per video.
